---
# What ansible-lint is allowed to decide here, and what it is not.
#
# The default profile is kept. Only the rules that contradict a decision this
# repository made on purpose are listed below, each with the reason, because a
# silent skip_list is how a project ends up with no standards at all.

skip_list:
  # var-naming[no-role-prefix] wants every variable set inside a role to carry
  # that role's name as a prefix: was_install_repository, model_cell_name,
  # server_member_cluster_name. It is good advice for a library of independent
  # roles. It is wrong here, and following it would break the architecture.
  #
  # The names of WAS objects are SHARED. was_cell_name means one thing across
  # the whole collection: the cell this run builds. profile_dmgr writes it into
  # a response file, the cluster job passes it to wsadmin, the audit role
  # compares it. That is the subject of README section 17 - one mechanism, one
  # name, no second rule - and the bug it exists to prevent is exactly the one
  # this rule would reintroduce: the same object named differently in different
  # places. A was_install_cell_name and a model_cell_name are two names for one
  # cell, and they will disagree.
  #
  # 168 of the 205 findings were this rule. Prefixed names are still used where
  # a variable really is role-local: server_member_weight, profile_node_ports,
  # model_allow_production.
  - var-naming[no-role-prefix]

# Advisory, not skipped: the later-wave roles are still stubs that fail on
# purpose, and a stub has no tasks to lint properly. The CI job keeps
# allow_failure until the whole collection is implemented, at which point it
# becomes a gate like the others.
